WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:02.620
Mario is a hero, right?

00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:04.960
Savior of the Mushroom Kingdom, beloved by
millions.

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.460
Who doesn't crack a smile when they see this?

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:09.590
"It's a-me, Mario!"

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:10.840
Don't be fooled.

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:14.840
Underneath that red hat and bushy moustache
lies an absolute monster.

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:17.180
Okay, maybe not an absolute monster.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:21.210
But Mario's got a few drybones in his closet
when it comes to being kind of a videogame

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:22.210
creep.

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:26.269
In fact, Mario's penchant for cruelty has
been right in front of our faces for decades,

00:00:26.269 --> 00:00:28.910
and it's time we called it out, for all to
see.

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:34.660
Super Mario Odyssey, Mario's next big opportunity
to redeem himself, will be out in winter 2017.

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:38.870
Let's review why Mario has been a menace for
over 35 years.

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:40.040
Animal cruelty

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:44.530
Donkey Kong's reign of terror against Mario
isn't just the big ape giving in to his animal

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:45.530
nature.

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:50.010
Sometime before the events of the original
Donkey Kong, Mario ran a circus, and his pet

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:51.740
Kong was the main attraction.

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:56.480
In the Game &amp; Watch title Donkey Kong Circus,
players control a captive Donkey Kong while

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:58.300
a menacing Mario watches.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:03.050
Kong is forced to roll left and right on a
barrel, juggling pineapples while also avoiding

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:04.050
fireballs.

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:05.300
Just look at Donkey Kong's face.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:07.220
Every moment of this is pure torture.

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:11.031
Sooner or later the player — and therefore
Kong — is going to mess up, and that's when

00:01:11.031 --> 00:01:13.360
Mario's cruelty is on full display.

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:18.380
When Kong drops a pineapple or gets scorched
by a fireball, Mario heartlessly points and

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:19.380
laughs.

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:20.990
This is animal cruelty, plain and simple.

00:01:20.990 --> 00:01:23.440
No wonder Donkey Kong wanted revenge.

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:25.100
Cruel and unusual punishment

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:29.690
Speaking of that revenge … after Mario saves
Pauline from Donkey Kong's clutches, he locks

00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:32.420
his nemesis in a cage and takes him prisoner.

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:35.940
That's understandable, considering the big
guy just kidnapped his girlfriend.

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:40.840
But when Kong's son tries to save him, Mario
goes...well...full-on supervillain to try

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:42.530
and kill a baby ape.

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:47.690
In Donkey Kong Jr., Mario sends vicious bear
traps, killer birds, and living electric sparks

00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:52.090
on a mission to maim and murder the young
gorilla … while his horrified father watches

00:01:52.090 --> 00:01:53.130
from his cage.

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:57.040
That's why it's so satisfying to see Papa
Kong kick Mario square in the face in the

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:58.350
game's final cutscene.

00:01:58.350 --> 00:01:59.350
Pow!

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:00.690
Right in the moustache.

00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:02.270
Brick buster

00:02:02.270 --> 00:02:04.170
You've seen Mario shatter blocks, right?

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:06.770
Aside from jumping, it's pretty much his signature
move.

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:11.420
What if we told you every time that Mario
breaks a block, he's actually taking a life?

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:12.420
It's true.

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:16.510
In the manual for the original Super Mario
Bros., Nintendo explains that when the Koopa

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:19.370
invaded the Mushroom Kingdom and took Princess
Peach hostage ...

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:24.340
"... the quiet, peace-loving Mushroom People
were turned into mere stones, bricks" and

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:28.180
something called "field horse-hair" plants,
which appears to be a mistranslation, since

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:32.700
Nintendo changed it to "mushrooms" when the
game was re-released in Super Mario All Stars.

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:34.740
But the part about them getting turned into
bricks?

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:36.080
That didn't change.

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:40.010
So every time Mario leaps into the air and
punches a brick, he's killing one of the very

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:45.040
civilians he's set out to save … or consuming
them in mushroom form to grow into "Super

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:46.040
Mario."

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:47.910
If there's a coin inside the block, it's even
worse.

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:52.540
In those cases, not only is Mario murdering
mushroom folk, he's robbing their corpses,

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:53.540
too.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:54.850
Not a good look, Mario.

00:02:54.850 --> 00:02:55.850
Mario the Lothario

00:02:55.850 --> 00:03:00.410
For a short, fat guy with ill-advised facial
hair, Mario really gets around.

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:04.480
After Donkey Kong, Mario ditched Pauline for
Peach, and while she's been his main squeeze

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:07.970
ever since, Peach isn't the only princess
in Mario's life.

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:11.800
In Super Mario Land, he enjoys a brief fling
with Princess Daisy.

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:15.910
That's right: the woman who's portrayed as
Luigi's boo in games like Mario Tennis, NES

00:03:15.910 --> 00:03:20.900
Open Tournament, and Mario Kart actually made
her big debut as Mario's side piece.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:25.590
In Super Mario Land, after besting the evil
Tatanga in a one-on-one dogfight, Mario and

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:29.500
Daisy hop into Mario's plane for a romantic
cruise through the clouds.

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:34.200
In the end-game cinematic, Mario and Daisy
embrace, and a single heart floats above their

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:35.200
heads.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:36.200
Face it, folks.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:38.710
Mario is a player...and a terrible brother.

00:03:38.710 --> 00:03:40.050
Brotherly shove

00:03:40.050 --> 00:03:43.280
If anyone has suffered at Mario's hands, it's
his brother Luigi.

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:47.530
When there's a second player around, Luigi
works just as hard as his older sibling, but

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:49.060
gets nowhere near the credit.

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:52.490
And when Luigi finally got to star in his
own adventure for the first time?

00:03:52.490 --> 00:03:56.970
It was a dreaded "edutainment" game — with
Mario's name, not Luigi's, in the title.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:58.739
What a slap in the face.

00:03:58.739 --> 00:04:03.660
Even worse, in Super Mario Sunshine, Mario,
Peach, and some Toads go on vacation, but

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:05.319
don't even invite Luigi.

00:04:05.319 --> 00:04:09.850
So, when Luigi finally wins it all in Mario
Power Tennis, the celebration is a long time

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:12.250
coming — until Mario ruins it.

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:17.749
First, Mario crashes the stage, Kanye-style,
then he slaps Luigi on the back a few times...before

00:04:17.749 --> 00:04:18.249
doing this:

00:04:22.430 --> 00:04:23.420
What a sicko.

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:24.819
Watch your back, Mario.

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:25.600
Luigi is coming for you.

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:30.600
Dino-slaughter

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:32.820
Imagine, for a second, that you are Yoshi.

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:37.189
You and your family worked to return two lost
babies to their parents, even though the little

00:04:37.189 --> 00:04:44.520
ones are being chased by monsters and they
make the most annoying sounds of all time.

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:49.139
Decades later, an evil turtle in a flying
clown head takes over your homeland, captures

00:04:49.139 --> 00:04:53.300
your friends, and locks them up in castle
basements all over the world — and turns

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:54.300
you into an egg.

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:58.289
Later, a human saves you — and it happens
to be the same little boy you rescued so many

00:04:58.289 --> 00:05:01.610
years ago, all grown up and able to fend for
himself!

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:02.610
Amazing!

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:06.139
You'd think, maybe, he'd treat you with a
little respect, right?

00:05:06.139 --> 00:05:07.139
Wrong.

00:05:07.139 --> 00:05:08.139
Want proof?

00:05:08.139 --> 00:05:12.330
Throughout the series, Mario jumps off of
Yoshi's back while his dino pal is jumping,

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:14.139
letting him do a sort of mega jump.

00:05:14.139 --> 00:05:18.889
That's good for Mario, but often works out
pretty bad for Yoshi, given that the dino-sacrifice

00:05:18.889 --> 00:05:23.129
usually happens while the pair are hovering
over a bottomless pit or a pool of lava.

00:05:23.129 --> 00:05:27.050
Don't let Mario off the hook by assuming Yoshi
magically comes back to life, either.

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:31.650
As Yoshi's Island confirmed, there are many,
many Yoshis out there, so that twisted creep

00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:35.360
Mario is probably just offing them one by
one until there are none left.

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:42.860
Mario's taste for mayhem is clearly insatiable.

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:44.220
Thanks for watching!

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:46.889
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:46.889 --> 00:05:49.180
Plus check out all this other cool stuff we
know you'll love!

